.TH LPUI 1 "2026-10-18" "lazyplan-tui 0.8.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lpui \- terminal issue tracker and roadmap planner for humans and coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lpui
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR [\fICOMMAND OPTIONS\fR]]
.br
.B lazyplan
is the same program under its long name.
.br
With no COMMAND, \fBlpui\fR launches the Textual TUI (same as \fBlpui ui\fR).
.SH DESCRIPTION
lazyplan tracks projects > stories > tasks in a per\-repo SQLite database. Humans drive the keyboard\-first Textual TUI; coding agents drive the same database through this CLI with \fB\-\-actor NAME\fR and \fB\-\-json\fR. Every mutation appends a feed event; the running TUI polls and toasts arrivals.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-db PATH
sqlite path (default: $LAZYPLAN_DB, else \./\.plan/ in repo, else global)
.TP
.B \-\-json
agent\-friendly JSON output
.TP
.B \-\-version
print the installed version and exit
.TP
.B \-\-actor NAME
who is making this change (surfaced in feed; default: $USER or 'human')
.SH COMMANDS
Flags work before or after the verb: \fBlpui list \-\-json\fR == \fBlpui \-\-json list\fR. Run \fBlpui COMMAND \-\-help\fR for details.
.TP
.B lpui init
init \.plan/ in this repo (or global db)
